{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/b29kza94","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":48,"top":105.6,"width":864,"height":33.6},"name":"Text 2","text":"Problem Statement","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":26.67,"typeface":"Calibri","color":"#1F4788","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/a10jqpsj","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":67.2,"top":148.8,"width":825.6,"height":144},"name":"Text 3","text":"Patients may take medicines from several prescribers, with mixed names and incomplete lists.\nClinicians need to spot interactions, duplicate therapy and patient-specific risks.\nMissed serious issues can harm patients. Too many minor alerts can hide urgent ones.","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":20,"typeface":"Calibri","color":"#303030","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/x4r21kru","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":48,"top":307.2,"width":864,"height":33.6},"name":"Text 4","text":"Market Opportunity","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":26.67,"typeface":"Calibri","color":"#1F4788","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/w3i1sfa9","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":67.2,"top":350.4,"width":825.6,"height":124.8},"name":"Text 5","text":"Initial users: clinicians and pharmacists reviewing patients on several medicines.\nProposed adoption: start with a small review workflow, then assess hospital integration.\nBaseline: manual reference lookups. Our aim is one prioritized, explainable review.","geometry":"rect","style":{"fontSize":20,"typeface":"Calibri","color":"#303030","alignment":"left"}}
